{"strongs": "H8147", "word": "שְׁנַ֫יִם", "translit": "she.na.yim", "root": "שנה", "morph": "H:N", "pos": "noun masculine and feminine dual", "gloss": "two", "definition": "שְׁנַ֫יִם , שְׁתַּיִם (Philippi ZMG xlix (1895), 202 Ges «GKC:97b»§ 97b note):768 noun masculine and feminine dual two (Late Hebrew id. ; Phoenician אשנם (and ׳ שנ second ), Punic שנם Lzb 380 ; Arabic ; Sabean תֿני Hom Chr 47 , Aramaic תְּרֵין , ( תִּנְיָנָא , second ); Nabataean תרין , Palmyrene feminine תרתן , תרתיא , Lzb 388 ; Assyrian šinâ; on etymology see √, and especially Philippi ZMG xxxii (1878), 21-98 ); — masculine (with masculine noun ) שְׁנַיִם Amos 3:3 +; construct שְׁנֵי Isa 7:16 +, suffix שְׁנֵיהֶם Gen 2:25 +, etc.; feminine (with feminine noun ) שְׁתַּיִם Amos 4:8 +; construct שְׁתֵּי Gen 4:19 , וּשְׁתֵּי Isa 7:21 +, etc., מִשְּׁתֵֿי Judg 16:28 (see GFM ); suffixes see below (2 + 10 = 12, see below); Hexateuch chiefly P ; — two: 1. no other number: \\ \\ a. usually construct before plural noun ( צְמִידִים ) שְׁנֵי Gen 24:22 + 19 t. + 2Sam 23:20 || 1Chr 11:22 (insert בְּנֵי ᵐ5 Th modern, otherwise RS Semitic i. 469, 2nd ed., 488 ); ( נָשִׁים ) שְׁתֵּי Gen 4:19 + 132 t., 1Sam 10:4 insert כִּכְּרוֺת Klo HPS Bu Now ; Lev 16:21 read dual יָדָיו Qr , + Judg 16:28 (see above) + שְׁתֵּיאֵֿלֶּה Isa 47:9 both these things ; before singular noun, שְׁנֵי Exod 16:22 ( Ges «GKC:134e»§ 134e ); suffix שְׁנֵיתֶם the two of them Gen 2:25 + 62 t., + Prov 24:22 (> their years ᵑ6 ᵑ7 De and others; probably corrupt, see Toy), שְׁנֵינוּ Gen 31:37 + 2 t., שְׁנֵיכֶם Gen 27:45 שְׁתֵּיהֶם (masculine suffix! Ges «GKC:135o»§ 135o ) Ruth 1:19 ; Ruth 4:11 , יֵ֯הֶן 1Sam 25:43 ; Ezek 23:13 . \\ \\ b. absolute (1) שְׁנַ֫יִם (90 t.), before plural noun Judg 11:37 + 26 t.; after plural noun 2Sam 1:1 ; Exod 29:1 + 21 t. (usually P Chronicles), singular noun (collective) Gen 46:27 ; Num 7:17 + 11 t. Num 17 noun omitted Gen 7:2 ; Gen 44:27 + 26 t.; ׳ שׁ ׳ שׁ distributive Gen 7:9 +; ׳ לִשׁ cut in two 2Kgs 3:25 ; Jer 34:18 = double amount Exod 22:3 ; Exod 22:6 ; Exod 22:8 ( E ); ׳ פִּי שׁ Deut 21:17 double portion , + בְּרוּחֲךָ 2Kgs 2:9 in (of) thy spirit , + בָּהּ Zech 3:18 (2) שְׁתַּ֫יִם (55 t.) before plural noun 1Kgs 3:16 + 16 t.; after plural noun (usually P and late) 2Chr 24:3 + 9 t.; noun omitted, = two things Isa 51:19 ; Job 13:20 ; Prov 30:7 שְׁתַּיִם = twice 2Kgs 6:10 ; Job 40:5 ; Ps 62:12 (or as Prov 30:7 ), ׳ בִּשׁ Job 33:14 either so, or in two ways RVm (see De ); as ordinal בִּשְׁנַת שְׁתַּיִם לְ 1Kgs 15:25 + 9 t., etc.; (3) as round number, שְׁנַיִם עֵצִים 1Kgs 17:12 a few sticks (German 'ein paar'), compare 2Kgs 9:32 ; Isa 17:6 שְׁתַּיִם שָׁלשׁ Amos 4:8 , פַּעַם וּשְׁתָּ֑יִם Neh 13:20 , compare Jer 3:14 אֶחָד מֵעִיר וּשְׁנַיִם מִמִּשְׁפָּחָה = a small number; Ezra 10:13 not for one or two days (but for many), 2Kgs 6:10 . 2. twelve: with noun masculine שְׁנֵים עָשָׂר Gen 42:13 + 87 t., לִשְׁנֵי עָשָׂר Exod 28:21 + 4 t.; with noun feminine שְׁתֵּים עֶשְׂרֵה Exod 24:4 + 34 t., שְׁתֵּי עֶשְׂרֵה Ezek 32:1 ; Ezek 32:17 ; Ezek 33:21 before plural noun Gen 17:20 ; Exod 15:27 +; after plural noun Num 7:84 (twice in verse) +; before singular noun Exod 28:21 +, Gen 14:4 (12 year ) +, etc.; as ordinal, יוֺם בְּיוֺם שְׁנֵים עָשָׂר Num 7:78 , בִּשְׁתֵּי עֶשְׂרֵה שָׁנָה Ezek 32:1 +, etc. 3. with larger number: 10 (etc.) + 2, 2Sam 8:5 ; Judg 10:3 + 56 t.; 2 + 10 (etc.) Num 1:35 ( P ), 2Chr 22:2 + 18 t. ( Kö ii. 1. 215 ff. Ges «GKC:97f»§ 97f .); 200 + 2 + 30, 1Kgs 20:15 50 + 2 as ordinal 2Kgs 15:27 + 2 t.; compare 2 + 20, 1Chr 24:17 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8886')\">BDB8886</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H8147')\">H8147</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8885')\">BDB8885</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8887')\">BDB8887</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>שְׁנַ֫יִם</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>שְׁתַּיִם</bdbheb> (Philippi<sup>ZMG xlix (1895), 202</sup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ges')\">Ges</lookup><sup>«GKC:97b»§ 97b</sup> note):768 <b>noun masculine and feminine dual</b> <highlightword>two</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>; Phoenician <bdbheb>אשנם</bdbheb> (and <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>שנ</bdbheb> <highlight>second</highlight>), Punic <bdbheb>שנם</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ldzb')\">Lzb<sup>380</sup></lookup>; Arabic <placeholder5640/>; Sabean <bdbheb>תֿני</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Hom')\">Hom<sup>Chr 47</sup></lookup>, Aramaic <bdbarc>תְּרֵין</bdbarc>, <placeholder5641/> (<bdbheb>תִּנְיָנָא</bdbheb>, <placeholder5642/> <highlight>second</highlight>); Nabataean <bdbheb>תרין</bdbheb>, Palmyrene feminine <bdbheb>תרתן</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>תרתיא</bdbheb>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ldzb')\">Lzb<sup>388</sup></lookup>; Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>šinâ;</highlight></transliteration> on etymology see √, and especially Philippi<sup>ZMG xxxii (1878), 21-98</sup>); — <div class=\"point\"><b>masculine</b> (with <b>masculine noun</b>) <bdbheb>שְׁנַיִם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Amos 3:3\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(30,3,3)\">Amos 3:3</ref> +; construct <bdbheb>שְׁנֵי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 7:16\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(23,7,16)\">Isa 7:16</ref> +, suffix <bdbheb>שְׁנֵיהֶם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 2:25\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(1,2,25)\">Gen 2:25</ref> +, etc.; <b>feminine</b> (with <b>feminine noun</b>) <bdbheb>שְׁתַּיִם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Amos 4:8\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(30,4,8)\">Amos 4:8</ref> +; construct <bdbheb>שְׁתֵּי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 4:19\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(1,4,19)\">Gen 4:19</ref>, <bdbheb>וּשְׁתֵּי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 7:21\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(23,7,21)\">Isa 7:21</ref> +, etc., <bdbheb>מִשְּׁתֵֿי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Judg 16:28\" b=\"7\" cBeg